# ── PER-CHUNK ATTRIBUTION (best-effort) ─────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. **bb39a784 + ddb94f27 + 4f626bd4 (W44-56 stage 7a-7d, Variable
#    predictor + cost-model refinement)** — closed the W44-54 photo
#    regression cluster. Evidence: 1418519 mean −1.64 % vs W44-56
#    baseline (it was +1.36 % vs W44-47 under W44-54); 1025469 mean
#    −1.67 % (photo win not present in W44-54/W44-55). Mechanism is
#    per-leaf Best(Gradient, Weighted) selection so the WP-better
#    smooth-photo leaves stop overpaying for the gradient predictor.
#
# 2. **b62d3462 (W44-57 per-stream kWPFixedDC)** — closed issue #57.
#    Routes the AC metadata stream through kWPFixedDC while DC stream
#    uses the learned tree. Likely contributor to codec_wiki −1.98 %
#    mean (AC metadata block context map reduction) and to the
#    1189261/1418519 wins on mid-d cells.
#
# 3. **cf30d2ed (W44-61 TryMergeAcs DCT64X32 non-aligned)** — closed
#    6 mid-band photo cells per its commit notes. In this sweep,
#    most visible on 1025469 d=3-5 and 1418519 d=3-5 (the top byte
#    wins of −3.0 % to −3.6 %).
#
# 4. **6169ba7b (W44-63 with_dct_suppress_hint opt-in)** — closed
#    codec_wiki e7 d=5 only when the caller passes
#    `with_dct_suppress_hint(true)`. In default-API path, hint is
#    None → byte-identical: codec_wiki e7 d=5 in W44-64 is still
#    bytes:+3.51% bfly:+4.11% (still OPEN). Confirms W44-63 is opt-in
#    only — production default unchanged. The W44-65 chunk should
#    wire auto-detection.
#
# 5. **5928aee2 (W44-59 AFV strategy-code remap)** — diagnostic-only,
#    no production code change. No byte-delta expected; no byte-delta
#    observed.
#
# 6. **deb20740 + 78ed46d3 + 93520d98 + 07f8b3d2 + 2af814dc** — all
#    docs/bench/cleanup. No byte deltas expected; no deltas observed.

