# ── W44-65 NEXT-ATTACK PROPOSAL ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Highest-EV next chunk: **codec_wiki e7 d=4,5,6 — wire the
# dct_suppress_hint auto-detection into the default API.**
#
# Rationale:
#   - W44-63 already SHIPPED the lever (`with_dct_suppress_hint`) and
#     proved it closes codec_wiki e7 d=5. The remaining work is the
#     content-aware *detection* heuristic so the default API picks
#     `Some(true)` for screenshot-like content at d>=4.
#   - Three cells closeable from one heuristic; codec_wiki tail is the
#     ONLY non-F-D OPEN cluster, so closing it puts the ledger at
#     pure F-D residual (17 cells, structurally bound per ruling).
#   - The W44-63 mechanism is identical in scope to the W44-22 /
#     W44-23 `content_aware_entropy_mul` workflow: detect screenshot-
#     class content via mask1x1 / palette_log2_size, opt into the
#     lifted suppression table. Reuse the same zenanalyze-driven
#     classifier (or a coarser mask1x1-only fast probe) instead of
#     adding a new classifier from scratch.
#   - Risk: same as `entropy_mul_smart_dispatch` — windows95-class
#     pixel-art may regress. Gate the detector with palette_log2_size
#     >= 6 (the W23-2 ruling) to avoid that class.
#
# Alternative (lower EV, longer horizon): F-D multi-feature
# discriminator for per-block RDO. Per f_d_residual_exhausted note
# this is the only path to crack the 17-cell F-D cluster, but it's a
# multi-week port (per-block libjxl RDO state-tracking on top of the
# AC strategy search). Not the right chunk to spawn while a 3-cell
# 1-week win sits on the table.
#
# Recommended W44-65 spec:
#   1. Sibling workspace `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-65-screenshot-dct-suppress`.
#   2. Read `vardct/effort.rs` (DCT64 suppress lever location from
#      W44-62) + `entropy_mul_smart_dispatch_ab.rs` (classifier shape
#      from W23-2 / chunk-1).
#   3. Implement `auto_dct_suppress_hint(features)` returning
#      `Option<bool>` (None = no change, Some(true) = lift on screenshots
#      with palette_log2_size >= 6, Some(false) = explicit off otherwise).
#   4. Wire into default API path at the same site `with_dct_suppress_hint`
#      currently consults the caller override.
#   5. A/B sweep all 10 GB82-SC screenshots + 8 ledger images at d=4,5,6
#      to confirm no regressions on photos.
#   6. Acceptance: 3 codec_wiki cells flip OPEN→FIXED, 0 cells flip
#      FIXED→OPEN on photos + windows95.
#
# Estimated effort: 1 work-day. Expected ledger delta: 20 OPEN → 17 OPEN
# (all photo F-D residual).
